From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] output: round the effective resolution instead of truncating

wlr_output_effective_resolution() divided width/height by output->scale
with a plain int /= double, which truncates toward zero. On panels whose
scale does not evenly divide their physical size (nuubOS gives every
720-wide built-in panel a 1.125 density scale, sized for the square
720x720 CubeXX: 480 / 1.125 = 426.666..., not 427 on the 720x480
RG34XX/RG SP family), every consumer of this truncated value
(labwc's output->usable_area, used for fullscreen/maximized view and
layer-shell geometry) disagreed with the panel's native resolution.
wlr_scene's scale_box() then rounds that logical height back up when
compositing a surface through it (round(426 * 1.125) = 479), one row
short of the panel's real 480: whichever surface goes through this path
(a game's fullscreen view, cropped/viewported for direct scan-out)
committed a scanout plane one line short of the ones that don't
(labwc's own composited output buffer, sized straight to the native
mode, no detour through this function), leaving the last line showing
a stale previous frame -- a thin, flickering line at the bottom
whenever the two disagreed (nuubOS report 2026-11-11, RG34XX/RG SP,
both 720x480; the square 720x720 CubeXX is unaffected since
720 / 1.125 = 640 exactly).

Round to the nearest integer instead: 480 / 1.125 rounds to 427, and
427 * 1.125 rounds back up to 480 in scale_box() too, so every consumer
agrees on the panel's real resolution again.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS
---
--- a/types/output/output.c
+++ b/types/output/output.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <drm_fourcc.h>
+#include <math.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <wlr/backend.h>
 #include <wlr/interfaces/wlr_output.h>
@@ -467,8 +468,15 @@ void wlr_output_transformed_resolution(struct wlr_output *output,
 void wlr_output_effective_resolution(struct wlr_output *output,
 		int *width, int *height) {
 	wlr_output_transformed_resolution(output, width, height);
-	*width /= output->scale;
-	*height /= output->scale;
+	/* nuubOS: round to the nearest integer instead of truncating. A
+	 * scale that does not evenly divide the panel's physical size (e.g.
+	 * 480 / 1.125 = 426.67) otherwise leaves every consumer of this
+	 * logical size (output->usable_area, layer-shell/view geometry) one
+	 * pixel short of what wlr_scene's own scale_box() rounds back up to
+	 * when compositing, producing an intermittent one-row-short scanout
+	 * commit (nuubOS report 2026-11-11, docs/dev/open-items.md). */
+	*width = (int)round(*width / output->scale);
+	*height = (int)round(*height / output->scale);
 }

 struct wlr_output_mode *wlr_output_preferred_mode(struct wlr_output *output) {
